  triage:title "AI22-BLOCK-005 closure did not satisfy the sprint doc's 'independent quality review' acceptance gate" ;
  triage:description "docs/plans/phase-ai/sprint-ai-22-loopback-self-send-exemption.md lines 160-163 require 'An independent quality review runs the release-built branch daemon through the real CLI and advertised-IP TCP listener... a mock router or direct-dispatch test cannot close this sprint.' AI22-BLOCK-005 was closed (see .triage/phase-AI/findings/AI22-BLOCK-005.ttl, triage:closureNote) on the basis of: (a) a same-commit, same-author (arch-ctm) evidence artifact at artifacts/phase-ai/ai22/advertised-ip-tls-self-send.md, and (b) quality-mgr (the same party performing the closure) reading that artifact and independently re-running cargo fmt/test/clippy -- which is not equivalent to a second, independent party actually executing the release-built daemon through the real CLI/advertised-IP TCP listener themselves. This is a compliance gap by construction: the acceptance criterion requires an independent execution of the live proof, not a same-party review of someone else's self-reported log plus a unit-test rerun. Confirmed by an independent req-qa review pass (2026-07-26) reading the actual artifact and sprint doc side by side." ;
